You would have to do a bit of R programming here.  First, for each treated unit, you can compute the number of matched controls.  This can be done by apply(!is.na(match.matrix), 1, sum).  Then, for each control unit, you check which treated unit it was matched to (you probably need to use a loop and "%in%"). 

Kosuke

